@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT domain

-- g7-administrative-courts.l4: section 62 of the Regulation of Engagement in Work on Refrigeration or
-- Air-Conditioning Systems Law 5785-2025, which amends the Administrative Courts Law.
--
-- Written by ENCODER G7.  Imports only `prelude` and `domain`.
--
-- Section 62 amends another statute, which is OUT OF SCOPE (the brief): what the Administrative Courts Law then
-- does with a decision under this Law enters as an input fact.  What is encoded is only what the added words say
-- (the Law is listed in item 21 of that statute's First Schedule), and the one place where the two statutes meet
-- (trap T39): section 56 sends a final decision of the Commissioner under Chapter 6 to the Magistrates' Court, and
-- section 62 on its face lists the whole Law, so the same decision has two candidate courts.  The Law does not say
-- which governs; the two readings are two callable functions (fork F-A-1 in FRAGMENT-G7.md) and neither is the
-- answer of the Law.
-- Section 56 itself belongs to G6; here it is taken from the wiki line quoted below, only to name the route.
--
-- Not gated on commencement (trap T20): section 63(a) fixes a commencement only "for the performance of work".

§ `Chapter 7 — Miscellaneous provisions: the Administrative Courts Law (section 62)`

§§ `62. Amendment of the Administrative Courts Law (No. 148)`

-- The wiki says only that the text was incorporated into the Administrative Courts Law.  The gazette prints the
-- amendment on printed page 198 (page image viewed; the text layer is scrambled and is not quoted).  In words (my
-- translation of the page image, not a quotation): in the First Schedule to the Administrative Courts Law,
-- 5760-2000, in item 21, add at the end "(31)" followed by the name of this Law.
-- src:456 | {{ח:סעיף|62|}}
-- src:457 | {{ח:ת}} {{ח:הערה|הנוסח שולב {{ח:חיצוני|חוק בתי משפט לעניינים מינהליים|בחוק בתי משפט לעניינים מינהליים, התש״ס–2000}}.}}
@ref s.62 (src:456-457); gazette printed page 198
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Law is listed in item 21 of the First Schedule to the Administrative Courts Law, as section 62 adds it` MEANS TRUE

@ref s.62 (src:456-457); gazette printed page 198
@desc The courts to which a decision under the Law can be taken: the Magistrates' Court under section 56 and an Administrative Court under the Administrative Courts Law as section 62 amends it
DECLARE `Forum for review of a decision under the Law` IS ONE OF
    `the Magistrates' Court, on appeal under section 56`
    `an Administrative Court, under the Administrative Courts Law as section 62 amends it`

-- Whether the Administrative Courts Law gives an Administrative Court jurisdiction over a decision of a kind its
-- First Schedule lists is for that statute (item 21, and its own sections), which is out of scope: it is the input
-- `the Administrative Courts Law gives an Administrative Court jurisdiction over the decision`.
@ref s.62 (src:456-457); gazette printed page 198
GIVEN `the decision was made under the Law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the decision was made under the Regulation of Engagement in Work on Refrigeration or Air-Conditioning Systems Law
      `the Administrative Courts Law gives an Administrative Court jurisdiction over the decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The effect of the Administrative Courts Law on a decision of a kind listed in item 21 of its First Schedule, supplied by the caller because that statute is outside this encoding
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 62 — the decision can be taken to an Administrative Court` `the decision was made under the Law` `the Administrative Courts Law gives an Administrative Court jurisdiction over the decision` MEANS
        `the decision was made under the Law`
    AND `the Law is listed in item 21 of the First Schedule to the Administrative Courts Law, as section 62 adds it`
    AND `the Administrative Courts Law gives an Administrative Court jurisdiction over the decision`

-- Section 56(a), the route it names, is quoted for the citation only; its 45 days belong to G6.
-- src:416 | {{ח:תת|(א)}} על החלטה סופית של הממונה לפי {{ח:פנימי|פרק ו|פרק זה}} ניתן לערער לבית משפט השלום שבו יושב נשיא בית משפט השלום, בתוך 45 ימים מיום שנמסרה הודעה על ההחלטה.
@ref s.56(a) (src:416); s.62 (src:456-457)
GIVEN `the decision is a final decision of the Commissioner under Chapter 6` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the decision is a final decision of the Commissioner under Chapter 6 of the Law
      `the decision can be taken to an Administrative Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The answer of the rule for section 62 above
GIVETH A LIST OF `Forum for review of a decision under the Law`
`the fora for review of a decision, reading section 62 as additional to section 56` `the decision is a final decision of the Commissioner under Chapter 6` `the decision can be taken to an Administrative Court` MEANS
    append
        (IF   `the decision is a final decision of the Commissioner under Chapter 6`
         THEN LIST `the Magistrates' Court, on appeal under section 56`
         ELSE EMPTY)
        (IF   `the decision can be taken to an Administrative Court`
         THEN LIST `an Administrative Court, under the Administrative Courts Law as section 62 amends it`
         ELSE EMPTY)

@ref s.56(a) (src:416); s.62 (src:456-457)
GIVEN `the decision is a final decision of the Commissioner under Chapter 6` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision can be taken to an Administrative Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `Forum for review of a decision under the Law`
`the fora for review of a decision, reading section 56 as the only route for a final decision of the Commissioner` `the decision is a final decision of the Commissioner under Chapter 6` `the decision can be taken to an Administrative Court` MEANS
    IF   `the decision is a final decision of the Commissioner under Chapter 6`
    THEN LIST `the Magistrates' Court, on appeal under section 56`
    ELSE IF   `the decision can be taken to an Administrative Court`
         THEN LIST `an Administrative Court, under the Administrative Courts Law as section 62 amends it`
         ELSE EMPTY
